From: Dynamic Devices <info@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] Build the companion graph-partition helper with simple_delegate

The product's Bazel-built TensorFlow Lite library does not export the delegate
GraphPartitionHelper implementation. Build its companion utility from the same
pinned TensorFlow source as simple_delegate.cc, rather than introducing another
TensorFlow runtime or accepting unresolved symbols in the delegate.

Strict linking is a target option, preserving all Yocto linker/hardening flags.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product TensorFlow provider integration]

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ endif()
 list(APPEND NEUTRON_DELEGATE_SRCS
   ${TFLITE_SOURCE_DIR}/delegates/utils/simple_delegate.cc
+  ${TFLITE_SOURCE_DIR}/delegates/utils.cc
   ${DELEGATE_SRC_DIR}/neutron_delegate.cc
   ${DELEGATE_SRC_DIR}/neutron_delegate_adaptor.cc
   ${DELEGATE_SRC_DIR}/neutron_delegate_dmabuf.cc
 )
@@ -113,2 +114,3 @@
 target_compile_options(${NEUTRON_DELEGATE_TARGET} PUBLIC ${NEUTRON_DELEGATE_OPTIONS})
+target_link_options(${NEUTRON_DELEGATE_TARGET} PRIVATE "-Wl,--no-undefined")
 target_link_libraries(${NEUTRON_DELEGATE_TARGET} PUBLIC ${NEUTRON_DELEGATE_DEPENDENCIES})
